    "turn_text": "Well, again, we're just to mention this weaponization of government. Part of that is, again, I think what the American people now clearly see, what so many constituents talk to me about, which is the double standard, the unequal application of the law, which is not supposed to happen in America. It's supposed to be equal treatment under the law, and it's supposed to be adherence to the Constitution and in fundamental principles of due process. But you can see this with these classified documents. There's one standard for Clinton and Biden. a different standard of your name is probably yesterday's is a wall street journal article that talked about uh... the fb i considered having agents a company biden lawyers when they were looking for classified documents that these various location and then they say oh no no we're not going to do that meanwhile they do you know they kick in the door and they read the home of president twelve ninety one day before the midterm election uh... i i still remember when when secretary clinton was in it during the big office meeting during week we we proposed to her we said hey look you've got sixty-some thousand emails on your on your personal uh... server uh... we don't need to see your personal emails we don't want to see that this is america you have a right to privacy we're going to protect that right but we we don't exactly trust you in your lawyers to give us to give us what we're entitled to see what what you know if there's a government work related emails so how about this option how about we have a uh... and neutral examine those emails and let that person decide which which are personally we shouldn't see which one to work related and of course she he or lawyer said no we're not doing that well that that that that courtesy wasn't even extended to present trump it was like no you don't get inside you and your lawyers no you don't get to have a neutral third party we're just coming in right in your home with being in cameras and helicopters flying around marlogo so that double standard is i think the biggest take away people now see what this with this part by document issue",
