    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "You got to put in some structural changes. You can't just raise it without. Here's a simple example. Why in the world should we raise the debt filling without the Senate actually passing a budget, something to have it done and who knows how long? So for goodness sake, if you're going to borrow more money, put the nation in greater debt, at least tell the country how you're going to spend that money. So do a budget. That's one simple thing. We should also put in place, if we get to the end of the fiscal year and we haven't agreed on the funding levels for the government, there shouldn't be a shut down uh... scenario play out we should say okay automatically we're going to spend at the current spending your level so if we can't get an agreement we're just going to spend it where we're at how about that i mean book all kind we have to do that they don't do they don't just get to go just keep spending more they have to set a budget they have to like sometimes live with the same the same amount of money in fact many american families this year arcy getting by was less because inflation has been at a record high those are just a couple of structural things i think make sense and finally i would say this earlier this week the white house that uh... pre john here said that oh no we're not going to negotiate with house republic really just at one point seven trillion dollars with virtually no republican support now on a bill uh... three-and-a-half weeks ago and and that we didn't vote for and they're saying oh yeah but you just got to automatically borrow more money so we can fund the bill that we didn't vote for that makes no sense",
